omething  while they're in sort of a holding  pattern they've considered and they've  talked about  but i don't really think it's anything  that's going to happen the other two  options are by far the preferred ones  with plan a and plan b as well there is  really a big push from amazon they want  to do sort of like a marvel style phases  that the movies tv series games and  other projects that if this is  successful they want to bring online  will all sort of mingle together and  you'll have bad guys that appear in the  movie the tv series etc across all the  things in phases like marvel so we might  have a phase of three or four years  building up towards something quite big  that will then  influence all of the projects at the  same time and then after that move on to  something else now imagine initially  that would be something like a gold bad  guy or something along those lines or  the lucian alliance  it will build up to some a big dramatic  finale  probably in a movie and then move on to  something new after that so what do i  think will happen  i think planet is by far the option i  prefer i'd love brad right to stay  involved um and like i said there is  another development that is very  interesting that i'll talk about in  another video  i'd love there to be a big movie to  really kick start this off in a really  big bang way  i don't mind if it's a tv series then if  that's successful follow up with a movie  or another series i love the idea of  this phased idea as well of building up  to some big finale and then moving on to  something else in a sorry a marvelous  style  i don't like the plan c i don't like  this option of a hard reboot but i i can  understand why it would be considered at  very least because in lots of  storytelling ways it's much easier  but i completely agree with the amazon  and mgm people that i've spoken to and  that they are really at risk of  alienating the audience if they do that  so please get in the comments tell me  what do